Title: {{ title }}
Policy ID: {{ policy_id }}
Owner: {{ document_owner }}
Department: {{ department }}
Effective Date: {{ effective_date }}
Version: {{ version }}
Status: {{ status }}
Applicable Regions: {{ applicable_regions | join(', ') }}
Approval Body: {{ approval_body }}
{% if supersedes %}
Supersedes: {{ supersedes }}
{% endif %}

1. Purpose
{{ purpose }}
This policy establishes the standards and requirements for {{ policy_area }} at HYTech Solutions.

2. Scope
This policy applies to {{ employee_type }} employees in {{ applicable_regions | join(' and ') }}.
All covered employees must comply with this policy from the effective date forward.
Contractors and temporary staff are subject to equivalent requirements unless explicitly exempted.

3. Eligibility
{{ eligibility_intro }}
- Minimum tenure: {{ min_tenure_months }} months
- Employee classification: {{ employee_type }}
- Applicable regions: {{ applicable_regions | join(', ') }}
{% if has_region_clause %}
- Employees in {{ region_clause_region }} are subject to local statutory minimums that may exceed the values stated in Section 4.
{% endif %}

4. Policy Statement
{{ policy_statement }}
The standard entitlement under this policy is {{ entitlement_value }} {{ entitlement_unit }}.
{% if has_enhanced_entitlement %}
Employees in {{ enhanced_region }} receive an enhanced entitlement of {{ enhanced_value }} {{ entitlement_unit }} in compliance with local regulations.
{% endif %}
All entitlements are subject to the eligibility criteria in Section 3 and the approval process in Section 5.

5. Procedure
{% for step in steps %}
{{ loop.index }}. {{ step }}
{% endfor %}

6. Exceptions
{% if has_exceptions %}
{{ exception_intro }}
The following exceptions to the standard policy are recognised:
{% for exc in exceptions %}
- {{ exc }}
{% endfor %}
Exceptions must be documented and retained by the HR Operations team for a minimum of {{ exception_retention_years }} years.
{% else %}
No exceptions apply to this policy. All employees in scope must adhere to the standard entitlement.
{% endif %}

7. Manager Responsibilities
Managers are responsible for:
- Approving requests within {{ manager_approval_days }} business days
- Ensuring compliance with this policy across their direct reports
- Escalating non-standard cases to the {{ escalation_contact }} before approval
- Maintaining accurate records in the HR information system

8. Employee Responsibilities
Employees must:
- Submit requests via the HR self-service portal at least {{ notice_days }} business days in advance
- Obtain written approval from their direct manager before confirming arrangements
- Notify the {{ escalation_contact }} if circumstances change after approval

9. Escalation
Unresolved queries should be directed to the {{ escalation_contact }}.
Escalations must be submitted in writing and acknowledged within 2 business days.
Disputes that cannot be resolved within 10 business days will be referred to the {{ approval_body }}.

